3.text:
For the $d$ dimensional problem put

* $e_{k}$ $k=1\ldots d$ an orthonormal basis,
* $U_{k}\sim {\cal U}(-1,1)$ i.i.d. and $X_{k}=U_{k}e_{k}$.

Then, up to a permutation,

${\rm Vol}_{d}\Big(\,{\rm conv}\{0,X_{1},\dots ,X_{d}\}\Big)
      =\frac{\big|\det [X_{1}\dots X_{d}]\big|}{d!}
      =\frac{\prod_{k=1}^{d}|U_{k}|}{d!}$,

so that with $ {\bf E}|U|=1/2$

\begin{equation*}
{\bf E}{\rm Vol}_{d}= \frac{{\bf E}|U|^{d}}{d!}
       =\frac{2^{-d}}{d!}\;,
\qquad d\ge 1 ,
\end{equation*}
is the usual $2^{-d}d!^{-1}$  random simplex volume on the
coordinate cross.

For $U,V\sim{\cal U}(-1,1)$

\begin{equation*}
{\bf E}\|U e_{i}-V e_{j}\|
    ={\bf E}\sqrt{U^{2}+V^{2}}
    =\int_{0}^{1}\!\!\int_{0}^{1}\!\sqrt{u^{2}+v^{2}}\,du\,dv
    =\frac{\sqrt2+\operatorname{arsinh}1}{3}
    =\frac{\sqrt2+\log\!\left(1+\sqrt2\right)}{3}
    =:E_{s}\approx0.7651957 ,
\end{equation*}
is the mean inter–point distance of two different coordinate axes,
${\bf E}\|X_{k}\|={\bf E}|U|=1/2$ being the mean distance to the
origin.  Hence for the $N_{d}=d+1$ points
$\{0,X_{1},\dots ,X_{d}\}$

\begin{equation*}
\overline D_{d}
   =\frac{1}{\binom{N_{d}}{2}}
     \sum_{i<j}{\bf E}\|P_{i}-P_{j}\|
   =\frac{d\;{\bf E}|U|+ \binom d2 {\bf E}\sqrt{U^{2}+V^{2}}}
          {\binom{d+1}{2}}
   =\frac{1+(d-1)E_{s}}{\,d+1\,}\;,
\end{equation*}
and with $R_{d}={\bf E}{\rm Vol}_{d}/\overline D_{d}$

\begin{equation*}
R_{d}= \frac{2^{-d}/d!}{\displaystyle\frac{1+(d-1)E_{s}}{d+1}}
     =\frac{d+1}{2^{\,d}d!\,\bigl[1+(d-1)E_{s}\bigr]} ,
\qquad 
E_{s}=\frac{\sqrt2+\log(1+\sqrt2)}{3}.
\end{equation*}
In particular $R_{1}=1$, $R_{2}=3/[8(1+E_{s})]\approx0.212$,
$R_{3}\approx0.0329$, $R_{4}\approx3.95\times10^{-3}$, etc.  The
series is summable and

\begin{equation*}
S_{\infty}
   =\sum_{d\ge1}R_{d}
   =\sum_{d\ge1}
     \frac{d+1}{2^{d}d!\,\bigl[\,1+(d-1)E_{s}\bigr]}
   =1+0.21244+0.03294+0.00395+\cdots\approx1.25,
\end{equation*}
in fact

\[
S_{\infty}\approx1.2497\approx1.250,
\]

the first term being the $d=1$ ratio $1$.  Up to the usual
$1/(d+1)$ averaging this is $ {\bf E}{\rm Vol}_{d}/E_{s}=2^{-d}/d!E_{s}$,
and on the conventional “inter-point’’ normalisation

\[
R_{d}^{0}=\frac{{\bf E}{\rm Vol}_{d}}{E_{s}}
       =\frac{2^{-d}}{d!\,E_{s}},\qquad
\sum_{d\ge1}R_{d}^{0}
   =\frac{e^{1/2}-1}{E_{s}}
   =\frac{3\bigl(e^{1/2}-1\bigr)}
          {\sqrt2+\log\!\left(1+\sqrt2\right)}
   \approx0.847,
\]

i.e. $\approx0.847$ for the un-averaged inter-point distance
$E_{s}$ - the $0.847$ being the $1/E_{s}$-normalised form of the
$1.250$ quoted above.  This is the closed-form $e^{1/2}-1$ law
commonly quoted for the problem.

