3.text:
With the cross

${\cal C}_{d}=\bigcup_{k=1}^{d}[-1,1]e_{k}$,
$X_{i}=r_{i}e_{K_{i}}$, $K_{i}\sim{\rm Unif}\{1..d\}$,
$r_{i}\sim{\rm Unif}[-1,1]$ i.i.d., put $P_{0}=0$, $P_{i}=X_{i}$,
$1\le i\le d$,

$E|r|=1/2$, $E|r_{1}-r_{2}|=2/3$ and

\begin{equation*}
I:=E\sqrt{r_{1}^{2}+r_{2}^{2}}
   =\int_{0}^{1}\!\!\int_{0}^{1}\!\sqrt{u^{2}+v^{2}}\,du\,dv
   =\frac{\sqrt2+\log\!\bigl(1+\sqrt2\bigr)}{3}
   \approx0.765195716\,,
\end{equation*}
so that for $i\ne j$

$E_{ij}:=E\|X_{i}-X_{j}\|
      =d^{-1}E|r_{1}-r_{2}|+(1-d^{-1})I
      =I-\frac{I-2/3}{d}\;,$
$E\|0-X_{i}\|=1/2$.

${\rm Vol}_{d}({\rm conv}\{0,X_{1}\dots X_{d}\})>0$ iff
$K_{1},\dots ,K_{d}$ is a permutation, ${\mathbb P}({\rm perm})=d!/d^{d}$,
and on the permutation event
$|\det[X_{1}\dots X_{d}]|=\prod_{i}|r_{i}|$.  Hence

\begin{equation*}
E V_{d}= \frac1{d!}E\!\left[\prod_{i}|r_{i}|
      {\bf1}_{{\rm perm}}\right]
       =\frac1{d!}\Big(\frac12\Big)^{d}\frac{d!}{d^{d}}
       =(2d)^{-d},\qquad EV_{1}=1/2 ,
\end{equation*}
$V_{1}=|r_{1}|$.

For the $N_{d}=d+1$ points $\{0,X_{i}\}$ the mean unordered pair
distance is

\begin{equation*}
D_{d}= \frac{dE\|X_{i}\|+\binom d2E_{ij}}{\binom{d+1}{2}}
     =\frac{1+(d-1)E_{ij}}{\,d+1\,}
     =\frac{1+(d-1)I+(d-1)(2/3-I)/d}{d+1}\!,
\end{equation*}
$D_{1}=1/2$, $\lim_{d}D_{d}=I$.

Hence the origin–inclusive ratio

\begin{equation*}
R_{d}:=\frac{EV_{d}}{D_{d}}
     =\frac{(2d)^{-d}(d+1)}
            {1+(d-1)E_{ij}}
     =\frac{(2d)^{-d}(d+1)}
            {1+(d-1)I+(d-1)(2/3-I)/d},
\end{equation*}
$R_{1}=1$, is $O\!\left((2d)^{-d}\right)$.  Numerically

\begin{array}{c|c}
d &R_{d}\\ \hline
1&1.000000\\
2&0.10927\\
3&0.00751\\
4&0.00038\\
5&1.5\times10^{-5}\\
\vdots&\vdots
\end{array}

and therefore

\begin{equation*}
S_{N}=\sum_{d=1}^{N}R_{d}
     =1+0.109270+0.007513+0.000379+\cdots
\end{equation*}
is extremely rapidly convergent.  In particular

$S_{\infty}=1.117178\ldots\approx1.117$,

i.e. $R_{1}=1$ and $\sum_{d\ge2}R_{d}\approx0.1172$, the $d=2$
contribution $R_{2}\approx0.1093$ dominating the tail.  Up to the
usual $d=1$ normalisation this is the $EV_{d}/D_{d}$ series for the
i.i.d. cross model.  On the pair–only normalisation $E\|X_{i}-X_{j}\|$
the series is $R_{d}^{\star}=(2d)^{-d}/E_{ij}$,
$\sum_{d\ge1}R_{d}^{\star}\approx0.844$, the familiar $3/4+0.0873+\dots$
form. ∎

